%description:

Tcp.rtoVarianceFloor:linux -- the minimum limits the variance term, as Linux.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: RTO = SRTT + max(4*RTTVAR, minRexmitTimeout), as Linux
(tcp_set_rto()), whose minimum limits the variance term".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and linux (true; LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::rttMeasurementComplete(). This test separates "linux" from "rfc".

Host under test: host1, with the minimum of 1 s, which sends 10000 bytes on a path with a
round trip of 100 ms. Observation: level 2, the signal rto after the first measurement is
0.1 + max(4 * 0.05, 1) = 1.1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.rtoVarianceFloor
%# class: linux
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.rtoVarianceFloor
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpRtoVarianceFloorLinux")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("rto")
                  .first()
                  .assertValueBetween(1.09, 1.12)
                  .describe("the RTO after the first measurement, SRTT plus the minimum")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpRtoVarianceFloorLinux compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.rtoVarianceFloor = true    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 25ms
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpRtoVarianceFloorLinux: PASS
